            "target_entity_type": "Metric",
            "paragraph": "Exposure to dangerous heat or heat extremes is assessed using summer heat danger hours (HDH), defined as the number of hours during the summer period that exceed the thermal danger threshold, which is calculated as HDH\u03b8 = \u03a3i=1n 1(WBGT > \u03b8 \u00b0C), where n is the total number of hours during the summer and where \u03b8 is the thermal danger threshold32.",
